    "public_output": "In the U.S. in 2020, the share of adults aged 18–64 who purchased online during shelter in place and planned to continue purchasing from a new online retailer in at least one category was 81%; separately, the share of adults aged 18–64 who participated in telemedicine/mobile health and viewed it as the same as or better than its in-person equivalent was 55%. These are distinct decision signals: stated retailer-continuation intent and perceived equivalence for a specific digital activity, not a single measure of durable digital demand. MarketLense would keep retention and digital-experience assessment separate, and treat the continuation figure as an intention to validate against later purchasing rather than an outcome.",
